dispositions.evidence:
New hwLow rule (js/aircraft/fit.js):
- keel-relative interpolation only when both sections reach dy and their bottoms differ by < 0.5;
- otherwise absolute height from the nearest sections that have skin there (a section whose bottom is above y is skipped, not counted 0).
I chose it by scoring 9 variants against planar cuts of the placed mesh.
New repo check tools/models/skin_check.mjs (the full-length scan the verifier asked for: 46 types, every 0.5 m, keel + 0.05..1.4 m), round 3 -> now:
- rows > 0.15 m off at keel + <= 0.3 m: 1045 -> 854; > 0.5 m: 688 -> 428;
- 737 family: 77 / 24, unchanged;
- A320 family: 136 / 126 -> 88 / 74;
- every height, > 0.5 m: 2237 -> 1587.
The verifier's cases now match the mesh:
- b77w X 61.5, keel + 1: 1.969 (mesh 1.981);
- a333 X 31: 2.189 (2.208);
- b788 X 28: 2.457 / 2.796 (2.465 / 2.808);
- a320 X 5.5: 1.597 (1.588).
The A319 aft door keeps the round-3 gain (0.39 vs mesh 0.44). Conveyor ends (belt_w2.mjs, both queries) are identical to round 3.

Not a defect; the residual is stated in the closeout as the verifier allowed. Object-level check on the verify2 tail-fit pickle against cuts of the fuselage object on the same side:
- the elevator's inboard end (root rib from X 36.05, |z| 0.39 L / 0.42 R, to X 37.16, |z| 0.14 / 0.17) is inside the cone, or within 0.02 m on the right side, whose source cone is 0.03 m narrower;
- the vertices counted 'outside' are the elevator's tab-cutout corners and the tab's own inboard end (|z| 0.43-0.54);
- these sit 0.17-0.25 m off the cone, with the elevator's inboard part between them and the skin. That is the artist's layout (0.31-0.36 m before the fit).
Clamping them would squash the tab. Tail-top previews show no gap or floating end. Stabiliser-root erratum (right side, 3 vertices up to 0.016 m outside) added.

Measured with the stabiliser row removed (var/NOSTAB):
- pitch: 737-600 / -700 / -800 / -900ER 1.49 / 1.29 / 1.02 / 0.91 deg nose-down (now 1.29 / 1.16 / 0.98 / 0.91); MAX -0.20 / -0.20 / -0.31 / -0.21 (now -0.12 / -0.14 / -0.22 / -0.12);
- dockSill: NG 2.703-2.719 (now 2.719-2.723), MAX 3.043-3.052 (now 3.033-3.041);
- every door row is within +-3 in either way.
The proper fix (stance on the doors, then dihedral alone to H / N) means re-converting the tailplane and re-baking every 737 livery again. It also moves T.Hc / dockSill while the round-3 realtime replays run against the current fit. The 7.0 deg dihedral is inferred; a primary value is needed (owner question).
Non-independence and the numbers are recorded in the fit.js STANCE_FIT comment, the types.js SPEC comment and the closeout.

